Using a generator in clean_tickets allows the script to
process support tickets lazily one at a time rather than
loading an entire data set into the memory. This reduces
memory usage and prevents system crashses when handling
massive log files.

In this script, a ticket line is considered "Malformed" if
it fails to split into exactly three separated parts:
The ID (T001,T002,T003,T004,T005), priority, and tags
or contains an invalid priority outside of "low, medium or high".
When a line breaks these rules, a custom error is raised
(TicketFormatError), allowing the generator to safely log
the issue, skip the bad line, and keep the code running.